{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WBvMcG4rfFHGbn5nUzJ7A2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '论文重心 80:20（分析:方法）。三层贡献：(1) pairwise confusability 跨 NER/RE/ED\n2\t  三任务、Qwen3+LLaMA 双模型成立， (2) multi-channel degradation model（count→omission, confusability→substitution）+\n3\t  错误分类学， (3) centrality confound 方法论发现 + 2×3 embedding ablation practitioner guidance。\n4\t  SDGD-zero 保留为 proof-of-concept 但 ΔF1 不显著（[-2,+2]pp），Claim 3 改写为 \"SDGD 框架示范 pairwise\n5\t  confusability 可直接指导 schema decomposition，SDGD-cal 预期有更大空间\"。 EMNLP Main 可冲（对标 Lost\n6\t  in the Middle），Findings 作后备。\n7\t\n8\t  '\n9\timagined_experiments:\n10\t- name: MAVEN Full Confusability Study\n11\t  plan_id: exp-004\n12\t  description: 'MAVEN 168 event类型，count curve + within-count BCS correlation + pairwise/per-type分析。\n13\t    跨任务验证（NER→ED），同域语义密集 schema 的 confusability 行为。\n14\t\n15\t    '\n16\t  expected_results:\n17\t    count_curve_relaxed_f1:\n18\t      count_1: 0.106\n19\t      count_6: 0.103\n20\t      count_12: 0.146\n21\t      count_22: 0.185\n22\t      count_44: 0.247\n23\t      count_64: 0.245\n24\t      count_168: 0.22\n25\t    count_curve_exact_f1:\n26\t      count_1: 0.009\n27\t      count_6: 0.003\n28\t      count_12: 0.008\n29\t      count_22: 0.013\n30\t      count_44: 0.018\n31\t      count_64: 0.013\n32\t    pairwise_minilm:\n33\t      pearson_r: 0.115\n34\t      pearson_p: 2.0e-34\n35\t      n_pairs: 11026\n36\t      spearman_rho: 0.098\n37\t      spearman_p: 1.5e-24\n38\t    pairwise_qwen3:\n39\t      pearson_r: -0.007\n40\t      pearson_p: 0.41\n41\t      verdict: NOT_SIGNIFICANT\n42\t    per_type_qwen3:\n43\t      spearman_rho: 0.189\n44\t      spearman_p: 0.021\n45\t      direction: POSITIVE (centrality confound)\n46\t    per_type_minilm:\n47\t      spearman_rho: 0.208\n48\t      spearman_p: 0.011\n49\t      direction: POSITIVE (centrality confound)\n50\t    within_count_bcs_relaxed_f1:\n51\t      count_6_r: 0.12\n52\t      count_6_p: 0.18\n53\t      count_12_r: 0.09\n54\t      count_12_p: 0.28\n55\t      verdict: FAIL — batch-level BCS confounded by centrality\n56\t    confusion_rate_ratio_extreme:\n57\t      count_6: 7.5\n58\t      count_12: 5.2\n59\t  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 168 类型全部来自 FrameNet 同域层级，语义空间高度同质（scs_mean=0.216， scs_std=0.103），导致两个层面行为分离：\n60\t    (1) Pairwise MiniLM 成立（r≈0.12）——因为 MiniLM 对细粒度事件类型对（如 Destroying↔Damaging） 的相对差异敏感，pair-level\n61\t    分析不受聚合效应影响； (2) Pairwise Qwen3 不显著——Qwen3 extraction-aligned embedding 在同域 schema\n62\t    中 将语义相近类型压缩到近乎相同的向量，丧失区分力； (3) Per-type 两种 embedding 均为正向 ρ≈+0.19/+0.21——这是 centrality\n63\t    confound： 在同质 schema 中 mean BCS 高的类型恰好是语义中心、高频类型，LLM 对其提取效果好。 这不是分析失败，而是方法论贡献——识别出\"per-type\n64\t    聚合在何时失效\"的具体机制。 Within-count batch-level 相关不显著，因为 batch-level BCS 范围被 schema 同质性压缩\n65\t    （0.87-0.94），区分度不足。\n66\t\n67\t    '\n68\t  tables:\n69\t  - name: 'Table: MAVEN Count Curve (Relaxed F1)'\n70\t    content: '| Count | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | Recall | Precision |\n71\t\n72\t      |-------|-----------|----------|--------|-----------|\n73\t\n74\t      | 1     | 0.106     | 0.009    | 0.142  | 0.083     |\n75\t\n76\t      | 6     | 0.103     | 0.003    | 0.130  | 0.085     |\n77\t\n78\t      | 12    | 0.146     | 0.008    | 0.172  | 0.127     |\n79\t\n80\t      | 22    | 0.185     | 0.013    | 0.210  | 0.165     |\n81\t\n82\t      | 44    | 0.247     | 0.018    | 0.268  | 0.229     |\n83\t\n84\t      | 64    | 0.245     | 0.013    | 0.255  | 0.236     |\n85\t\n86\t      '\n87\t  - name: 'Table: MAVEN Pairwise & Per-type Analysis (2×2 Embedding Matrix)'\n88\t    content: '| Level     | Qwen3          | MiniLM          |\n89\t\n90\t      |-----------|----------------|-----------------|\n91\t\n92\t      | Pairwise  | r=-0.007 (ns)  | r=+0.115 ✓      |\n93\t\n94\t      | Per-type  | ρ=+0.189 ✗     | ρ=+0.208 ✗      |\n95\t\n96\t      Note: ✓=supports confusability hypothesis, ✗=centrality confound direction\n97\t\n98\t      '\n99\t  figures_description:\n100\t  - 'Scatter plot: MiniLM pairwise SCS vs confusion count (11K pairs), with regression\n101\t    line r=0.115. Long tail of high-SCS pairs with elevated confusion.'\n102\t  - 'Bar chart: per-type mean BCS quartiles vs relaxed F1, showing positive trend\n103\t    (centrality confound). Annotated with frequency distribution per quartile.'\n104\t  - 'Heatmap: top-20 confused event type pairs, colored by MiniLM SCS. Diagonal stripe\n105\t    pattern showing FrameNet siblings.'\n106\t  analysis: 'MAVEN 为 pairwise confusability 提供跨任务复现（NER→ED），同时暴露 per-type 聚合的 centrality\n107\t    confound 机制。MiniLM pairwise r=0.115 与 Few-NERD r=0.156 量级一致， 但 Qwen3 在同域 schema\n108\t    上失效，证实\"embedding 选择影响信号检测\"的结论。 Per-type 正向 ρ 构成独立方法论贡献：当 schema 语义同质时，mean BCS\n109\t    不再是 confusability 的有效聚合指标，需回退到 pairwise level。\n110\t\n111\t    '\n112\t- name: DocRED Confusability Scaling Test\n113\t  plan_id: exp-005\n114\t  description: 'DocRED 96 relation types，count curve + BCS correlation。 文档级 RE 的 scaling\n115\t    stress test，验证 confusability 信号在更复杂抽取设置下是否成立。\n116\t\n117\t    '\n118\t  expected_results:\n119\t    count_curve_f1:\n120\t      count_1: 0.18\n121\t      count_6: 0.22\n122\t      count_12: 0.25\n123\t      count_24: 0.23\n124\t      count_48: 0.19\n125\t      count_96: 0.14\n126\t    pairwise_qwen3:\n127\t      pearson_r: 0.082\n128\t      pearson_p: 0.008\n129\t      n_pairs: 4560\n130\t    pairwise_minilm:\n131\t      pearson_r: 0.095\n132\t      pearson_p: 0.001\n133\t    per_type_qwen3:\n134\t      spearman_rho: -0.165\n135\t      spearman_p: 0.108\n136\t    within_count_bcs_f1:\n137\t      count_12_r: 0.18\n138\t      count_12_p: 0.12\n139\t      count_24_r: 0.25\n140\t      count_24_p: 0.065\n141\t  result_rationale: 'DocRED 是文档级 RE，96 relation types 跨越多域（人物、地理、组织等）， 语义异质性介于 Few-NERD（跨域\n142\t    NER）和 MAVEN（同域 ED）之间。 Pairwise 信号可检测（r≈0.08-0.10）但弱于 Few-NERD（r=0.156），原因是： (1)\n143\t    文档级 RE 噪声更大——同一文档多个 relation 共现，confusion 来源更复杂； (2) relation type 的语义相似性比 entity\n144\t    type 更抽象（\"country of citizenship\" vs \"place of birth\" 的 embedding 距离不完全反映 LLM\n145\t    的实际混淆模式）； (3) DocRED 的 distant supervision 标注本身有噪声，增加 metric variance。 Per-type\n146\t    方向一致（负 ρ）但因 n=96 types + 噪声，未达显著。 作为 P1 实验，主要贡献是\"第四个数据点\"但非必须——三任务已足够。\n147\t\n148\t    '\n149\t  tables:\n150\t  - name: 'Table: DocRED Count Curve'\n151\t    content: '| Count | F1    | Recall | Precision |\n152\t\n153\t      |-------|-------|--------|-----------|\n154\t\n155\t      | 1     | 0.180 | 0.280  | 0.133     |\n156\t\n157\t      | 6     | 0.220 | 0.290  | 0.178     |\n158\t\n159\t      | 12    | 0.250 | 0.275  | 0.229     |\n160\t\n161\t      | 24    | 0.230 | 0.240  | 0.221     |\n162\t\n163\t      | 48    | 0.190 | 0.195  | 0.185     |\n164\t\n165\t      | 96    | 0.140 | 0.135  | 0.146     |\n166\t\n167\t      '\n168\t  figures_description:\n169\t  - DocRED count curve overlay with Few-NERD (normalized F1), showing both exhibit\n170\t    inverted-U but DocRED peaks earlier (count_12 vs count_44).\n171\t  analysis: 'DocRED 提供第四个数据点但效应量衰减。如果时间紧张（ARR deadline 10 天）， 可降级为 appendix 或完全跳过——Few-NERD\n172\t    + FewRel + MAVEN 已覆盖 NER/RE/ED 三任务。\n173\t\n174\t    '\n175\t- name: Count × Confusability Interaction Effect\n176\t  plan_id: exp-006\n177\t  description: '2×2 factorial：{low count (6), high count (22)} × {low BCS, high BCS}，Few-NERD。\n178\t    检验 count 和 confusability 的交互是加性还是乘性。\n179\t\n180\t    '\n181\t  expected_results:\n182\t    cell_f1:\n183\t      low_count_low_bcs: 0.355\n184\t      low_count_high_bcs: 0.305\n185\t      high_count_low_bcs: 0.295\n186\t      high_count_high_bcs: 0.23\n187\t    main_effect_count:\n188\t      delta_f1_pp: -6.3\n189\t      f_stat: 8.2\n190\t      p_value: 0.007\n191\t    main_effect_bcs:\n192\t      delta_f1_pp: -5.8\n193\t      f_stat: 6.5\n194\t      p_value: 0.015\n195\t    interaction:\n196\t      f_stat: 1.4\n197\t      p_value: 0.24\n198\t      effect_size_eta2: 0.03\n199\t    model_comparison:\n200\t      additive_R2: 0.38\n201\t      multiplicative_R2: 0.39\n202\t  result_rationale: 'Count 和 confusability 通过不同通道降解性能：count 导致 recall 下降（omission），\n203\t    confusability 导致 precision 下降（substitution）。这两个通道大致正交—— 增加 count 不会显著放大 confusability\n204\t    的效应，反之亦然。 Interaction term 不显著（p≈0.24）的原因是：(1) 两通道作用于不同错误类型， 物理上近似独立；(2) 2×2 设计只有\n205\t    ~20 batches/cell，检测交互效应的统计功效有限。 Additive model 已解释 ~38% 方差，interaction 仅贡献 1%。\n206\t    这实际上支持 multi-channel model 的核心主张——count 和 confusability 可独立处理。\n207\t\n208\t    '\n209\t  tables:\n210\t  - name: 'Table: 2×2 Factorial Results'\n211\t    content: '|                | Low BCS  | High BCS | Marginal |\n212\t\n213\t      |----------------|----------|----------|----------|\n214\t\n215\t      | Low count (6)  | 0.355    | 0.305    | 0.330    |\n216\t\n217\t      | High count (22)| 0.295    | 0.230    | 0.263    |\n218\t\n219\t      | Marginal       | 0.325    | 0.268    |          |\n220\t\n221\t      '\n222\t  figures_description:\n223\t  - 'Interaction plot: two roughly parallel lines (low BCS, high BCS) across count\n224\t    levels, illustrating additive (not synergistic) effect.'\n225\t  analysis: '加性模型优于乘性模型但 margin 很小。关键 takeaway 是\"two independent knobs\"—— 从业者可以分别优化\n226\t    batch size（控制 count 通道）和 batch composition（控制 confusability 通道）， 无需考虑复杂交互。这是 practitioner\n227\t    guidance 的基础。\n228\t\n229\t    '\n230\t- name: Systematic Error Taxonomy\n231\t  plan_id: exp-007\n232\t  description: '跨 BCS bins 的 FP 系统分类：type_substitution / boundary_error / omission\n233\t    / hallucination。 为 multi-channel model 提供机制证据。\n234\t\n235\t    '\n236\t  expected_results:\n237\t    error_distribution_high_bcs:\n238\t      type_substitution_pct: 62\n239\t      boundary_error_pct: 14\n240\t      omission_pct: 18\n241\t      hallucination_pct: 6\n242\t    error_distribution_low_bcs:\n243\t      type_substitution_pct: 28\n244\t      boundary_error_pct: 22\n245\t      omission_pct: 42\n246\t      hallucination_pct: 8\n247\t    error_distribution_medium_bcs:\n248\t      type_substitution_pct: 45\n249\t      boundary_error_pct: 18\n250\t      omission_pct: 30\n251\t      hallucination_pct: 7\n252\t    substitution_ratio_high_vs_low: 2.2\n253\t    omission_ratio_low_vs_high: 2.3\n254\t    substitution_trend_with_count:\n255\t      count_6: 0.35\n256\t      count_12: 0.48\n257\t      count_22: 0.55\n258\t    omission_trend_with_count:\n259\t      count_6: 0.28\n260\t      count_12: 0.32\n261\t      count_22: 0.38\n262\t  result_rationale: 'Error taxonomy 是 multi-channel model 的直接机制验证。 High-BCS batches\n263\t    中 type_substitution 占主导（~62%）因为语义相似类型共现时 LLM 识别了正确的 span 但选错了类型标签——这正是 confusability\n264\t    channel 的定义。 Low-BCS batches 中 omission 占主导（~42%）因为虽然类型不相似但数量多， LLM 的 attention\n265\t    被分散，更多实体被完全遗漏——这是 count channel。 Substitution 随 count 增加（0.35→0.55）因为更多类型意味着更多潜在混淆对。\n266\t    Omission 也随 count 增加（0.28→0.38）因为 attention dilution 加剧。 两种错误都对 count 有响应，但 confusability\n267\t    只放大 substitution，不影响 omission—— 这是两通道正交性的直接证据。\n268\t\n269\t    '\n270\t  tables:\n271\t  - name: 'Table: Error Distribution by BCS Bin'\n272\t    content: '| Error Type       | Low BCS | Med BCS | High BCS |\n273\t\n274\t      |------------------|---------|---------|----------|\n275\t\n276\t      | Type Substitution| 28%     | 45%     | 62%      |\n277\t\n278\t      | Boundary Error   | 22%     | 18%     | 14%      |\n279\t\n280\t      | Omission         | 42%     | 30%     | 18%      |\n281\t\n282\t      | Hallucination    | 8%      | 7%      | 6%       |\n283\t\n284\t      '\n285\t  - name: 'Table: Error Rates by Count Level (All BCS)'\n286\t    content: '| Error Type       | Count 6 | Count 12 | Count 22 |\n287\t\n288\t      |------------------|---------|----------|----------|\n289\t\n290\t      | Substitution Rate| 0.035   | 0.048    | 0.055    |\n291\t\n292\t      | Omission Rate    | 0.028   | 0.032    | 0.038    |\n293\t\n294\t      '\n295\t  figures_description:\n296\t  - 'Stacked bar chart: error type composition across 5 BCS quintiles, showing substitution/omission\n297\t    crossover at BCS≈0.82.'\n298\t  - 'Dual-axis line chart: substitution rate (left axis) and omission rate (right\n299\t    axis) vs count, both increasing but substitution steeper.'\n300\t  analysis: 'Error taxonomy 将 \"confusability degrades extraction\" 的抽象主张具象化为可操作的诊断框架：\n301\t    看到 high substitution rate → confusability 问题 → SDGD-style decomposition； 看到 high\n302\t    omission rate → count 问题 → reduce batch size。 这本身是论文的独立贡献，特别是在 Claim 3 (SDGD gains)\n303\t    不显著的 median 档下， 错误分类学提供了\"分析即贡献\"的具体证据。\n304\t\n305\t    '\n306\t- name: LLaMA-3.3-70B Multi-Model Validation\n307\t  plan_id: exp-012\n308\t  description: 'LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 复现 exp-002 协议。 验证 confusability 信号的模型无关性——是\n309\t    schema 属性而非模型特异行为。\n310\t\n311\t    '\n312\t  expected_results:\n313\t    fewnerd_pairwise:\n314\t      pearson_r: 0.098\n315\t      pearson_p: 3.2e-05\n316\t      n_pairs: 1953\n317\t      spearman_rho: 0.105\n318\t      spearman_p: 8.7e-06\n319\t      nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.195\n320\t      nonzero_spearman_p: 0.0004\n321\t    fewnerd_per_type:\n322\t      spearman_rho: -0.215\n323\t      spearman_p: 0.089\n324\t      partial_r_ctrl_logfreq: -0.155\n325\t      partial_p: 0.225\n326\t    count_curve_f1:\n327\t      count_1: 0.285\n328\t      count_6: 0.27\n329\t      count_12: 0.305\n330\t      count_22: 0.265\n331\t      count_44: 0.38\n332\t      count_64: 0.355\n333\t    confusion_rate_ratio_extreme:\n334\t      count_6: 12.5\n335\t      count_12: 6.8\n336\t    batch_level_f1_vs_bcs:\n337\t      count_12_r: 0.38\n338\t      count_12_p: 0.045\n339\t  result_rationale: 'LLaMA-3.3-70B 复现 pairwise 信号（r≈0.10, p<0.001）但效应量小于 Qwen3（r=0.156），\n340\t    原因是： (1) LLaMA 和 Qwen3 架构不同（LLaMA 使用 GQA vs Qwen3 使用 GQA+SWA）， 对 prompt 中类型列表的\n341\t    attention 分配模式不同，导致 confusability 的表现形式有差异； (2) LLaMA-70B 参数量更大（70B vs 32B），可能对\n342\t    confusable types 有更强的区分能力， 从而压缩效应量； (3) 但 pairwise 信号方向一致且显著——confusability 是\n343\t    schema 结构属性， 不同模型都会受影响，只是程度不同。 Per-type ρ=-0.215 方向一致但 p=0.089 未达 0.05——这在 median\n344\t    档预期范围内 （cross_model_significant: [1,2]），pairwise 显著已足够支撑 multi-model claim。 Overall\n345\t    F1 水平比 Qwen3 低 5-10%，可能因 LLaMA 的 NER few-shot 能力略弱。\n346\t\n347\t    '\n348\t  tables:\n349\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-Model Pairwise Comparison'\n350\t    content: '| Metric              | Qwen3-32B   | LLaMA-3.3-70B |\n351\t\n352\t      |---------------------|-------------|---------------|\n353\t\n354\t      | Pairwise r          | 0.156       | 0.098         |\n355\t\n356\t      | Pairwise p          | 4.6e-12     | 3.2e-05       |\n357\t\n358\t      | Per-type ρ          | -0.293*     | -0.215        |\n359\t\n360\t      | Confusion ratio (6) | 27.5x       | 12.5x         |\n361\t\n362\t      | Confusion ratio (12)| 9.9x        | 6.8x          |\n363\t\n364\t      * p<0.05\n365\t\n366\t      '\n367\t  - name: 'Table: LLaMA Count Curve'\n368\t    content: '| Count | F1    | Recall | Precision |\n369\t\n370\t      |-------|-------|--------|-----------|\n371\t\n372\t      | 1     | 0.285 | 0.580  | 0.190     |\n373\t\n374\t      | 6     | 0.270 | 0.420  | 0.200     |\n375\t\n376\t      | 12    | 0.305 | 0.310  | 0.300     |\n377\t\n378\t      | 22    | 0.265 | 0.255  | 0.275     |\n379\t\n380\t      | 44    | 0.380 | 0.365  | 0.396     |\n381\t\n382\t      | 64    | 0.355 | 0.280  | 0.485     |\n383\t\n384\t      '\n385\t  figures_description:\n386\t  - 'Overlay scatter: Qwen3 vs LLaMA pairwise SCS-confusion, same axes. Both positive\n387\t    slopes, LLaMA shallower.'\n388\t  - 'Side-by-side confusion heatmaps (top-20 pairs): substantial overlap in confused\n389\t    pairs between models.'\n390\t  analysis: 'LLaMA 在 pairwise level 显著复现信号（r≥0.08, p<0.05），满足 median 档 cross_model_significant\n391\t    ≥1 的阈值。Per-type 未达显著但方向一致。 效应量差异本身是有意义的发现——更大的模型可能对 confusability 更鲁棒， 暗示 confusability\n392\t    降解是 training-free setting 的固有挑战，可通过 scaling 部分缓解但不消除。 论文中报告为\"cross-model replication\n393\t    with attenuated but significant effect\"。\n394\t\n395\t    '\n396\t- name: SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\n397\t  plan_id: exp-008\n398\t  description: 'Confusability-minimizing batch composition：embedding SCS 阈值化 → confusability\n399\t    graph → graph coloring → batches。对比 single-pass full-schema baseline。\n400\t\n401\t    '\n402\t  expected_results:\n403\t    sdgd_zero_config:\n404\t      embedding: qwen3\n405\t      threshold: 0.85\n406\t      n_batches: 8\n407\t      avg_batch_size: 8.25\n408\t      coloring_algorithm: greedy_dsatur\n409\t    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n410\t    singlepass_f1: 0.414\n411\t    delta_f1_pp: 1.1\n412\t    delta_f1_ci_95:\n413\t    - -1.5\n414\t    - 3.7\n415\t    p_value_paired_t: 0.18\n416\t    significant: false\n417\t    sdgd_zero_recall: 0.335\n418\t    sdgd_zero_precision: 0.58\n419\t    singlepass_recall: 0.304\n420\t    singlepass_precision: 0.648\n421\t    type_confusion_errors:\n422\t      sdgd_zero: 1850\n423\t      singlepass: 2434\n424\t      reduction_pct: 24\n425\t    omission_errors:\n426\t      sdgd_zero: 3200\n427\t      singlepass: 2850\n428\t      increase_pct: 12\n429\t    api_calls: 8\n430\t    wall_clock_ratio: 3.2\n431\t  result_rationale: 'SDGD-zero 在 median 档下 ΔF1≈+1.1pp，置信区间跨零，不显著。核心权衡： (1) Confusability\n432\t    降低的收益——分离 confusable types（如 person-other 和 person-politician 不再共现于同一 batch），type\n433\t    confusion errors 减少 ~24%，precision 改善； (2) 跨类型上下文丢失的代价——单 batch 只看到 ~8 个类型而非全部\n434\t    66 个， LLM 无法利用\"这不是 X 所以应该是 Y\"的排除推理，omission errors 增加 ~12%； (3) 这两个效应在 F1 层面大致抵消。Precision\n435\t    提升（0.648→0.580 actually下降... 不对，让我修正）——SDGD-zero 的 recall 高于 single-pass（0.335>0.304）因为\n436\t    smaller batches 意味着更少的 attention dilution，但 precision 降低因为 smaller batches 使模型缺少同\n437\t    batch 内的对比信号。 净效应：recall 提升 + precision 下降 → F1 微小提升但不显著。 这正是 median 档的核心判断——decomposition\n438\t    是可行的框架但不是 silver bullet。\n439\t\n440\t    '\n441\t  tables:\n442\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD-zero vs Single-pass on Few-NERD (66 types)'\n443\t    content: '| Method      | F1    | Recall | Precision | Type Confusion | Omission\n444\t      | API Calls |\n445\t\n446\t      |-------------|-------|--------|-----------|----------------|----------|-----------|\n447\t\n448\t      | Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.304  | 0.648     | 2434           | 2850     | 1         |\n449\t\n450\t      | SDGD-zero   | 0.425 | 0.335  | 0.580     | 1850           | 3200     | 8         |\n451\t\n452\t      | Δ           | +1.1  | +3.1   | -6.8      | -24%           | +12%     | +7        |\n453\t\n454\t      '\n455\t  figures_description:\n456\t  - 'Paired bar chart: error type breakdown for single-pass vs SDGD-zero, showing\n457\t    substitution↓ / omission↑ tradeoff.'\n458\t  - 'Scatter: per-batch F1 vs batch mean BCS for SDGD-zero batches, showing SDGD batches\n459\t    cluster at low BCS.'\n460\t  analysis: 'SDGD-zero 的价值不在于 F1 增益（不显著），而在于： (1) 验证 pairwise confusability 可直接转化为\n461\t    actionable decomposition； (2) 错误 profile 的定向转移证实 multi-channel model——confusability\n462\t    channel 可关闭（减 24% substitution）， 但代价是轻度激活 count channel（增 12% omission）； (3) 为\n463\t    SDGD-cal 提供 baseline——如果用 empirical confusion 替代 embedding proxy， graph 更准确，预期收益更大。\n464\t\n465\t    '\n466\t- name: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n467\t  plan_id: exp-009\n468\t  description: 'SDGD-zero 在 MAVEN 168 event types 上的跨任务验证。 同域高密度 schema 对 graph coloring\n469\t    的挑战。\n470\t\n471\t    '\n472\t  expected_results:\n473\t    sdgd_zero_config:\n474\t      embedding: minilm\n475\t      threshold: 0.35\n476\t      n_batches: 14\n477\t      avg_batch_size: 12\n478\t    sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.24\n479\t    singlepass_relaxed_f1: 0.245\n480\t    random_batching_relaxed_f1: 0.235\n481\t    delta_vs_singlepass_pp: -0.5\n482\t    delta_vs_random_pp: 0.5\n483\t    significant: false\n484\t    sdgd_zero_exact_f1: 0.015\n485\t    singlepass_exact_f1: 0.013\n486\t    api_calls: 14\n487\t  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 的同域同质 schema 对 SDGD-zero 极具挑战： (1) SCS 分布集中（mean=0.216,\n488\t    std=0.103），大部分 pair 相似度在 0.1-0.35 范围， 用阈值 0.35 切分后 confusability graph 边数较少，graph\n489\t    coloring 产生的 batches 与 random batching 差异不大； (2) 即使成功分离了高 SCS pairs（119 pairs\n490\t    > 0.5），这些 pairs 分布在 168 个 types 中仅占 0.85%，对整体 F1 影响微小； (3) Exact F1 极低（<0.02）使得任何方法差异都淹没在\n491\t    boundary matching 噪声中， relaxed F1 是唯一可比指标； (4) SDGD-zero 微弱优于 random batching（+0.5pp），但不优于\n492\t    single-pass（-0.5pp）， 因为 MAVEN 的 context 更重要——event detection 依赖同一句中多种事件类型的对比。\n493\t\n494\t    '\n495\t  tables:\n496\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD-zero vs Baselines on MAVEN (168 types)'\n497\t    content: '| Method          | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | API Calls |\n498\t\n499\t      |-----------------|-----------|----------|-----------|\n500\t\n501\t      | Single-pass     | 0.245     | 0.013    | 1         |\n502\t\n503\t      | Random (k=14)   | 0.235     | 0.012    | 14        |\n504\t\n505\t      | SDGD-zero       | 0.240     | 0.015    | 14        |\n506\t\n507\t      '\n508\t  figures_description:\n509\t  - 'MAVEN confusability graph visualization: near-complete subgraph structure, illustrating\n510\t    why graph coloring fails to find clean separations.'\n511\t  analysis: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-zero ≈ single-pass 进一步支持 median 档叙事： SDGD 是正确的框架但 -zero\n512\t    变体在高密度 schema 上能力有限。 这也解释了为什么 embedding-based proxy 不够——需要 empirical confusion\n513\t    data (SDGD-cal) 才能在同域 schema 上有效操作。\n514\t\n515\t    '\n516\t- name: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n517\t  plan_id: exp-010\n518\t  description: '用 5-10 calibration examples 的 empirical confusion matrix 替代 embedding\n519\t    SCS 构建 confusability graph。 检验 calibration 数据能否弥补 embedding proxy 的不足。\n520\t\n521\t    '\n522\t  expected_results:\n523\t    calibration_config:\n524\t      n_calibration_examples: 8\n525\t      calibration_api_calls: 528\n526\t      total_api_calls: 536\n527\t    sdgd_cal_f1: 0.44\n528\t    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n529\t    singlepass_f1: 0.414\n530\t    delta_cal_vs_zero_pp: 1.5\n531\t    delta_cal_vs_singlepass_pp: 2.6\n532\t    delta_cal_vs_singlepass_ci_95:\n533\t    - -0.8\n534\t    - 6.0\n535\t    p_value_vs_singlepass: 0.09\n536\t    significant_vs_singlepass: false\n537\t    type_confusion_reduction_vs_singlepass_pct: 35\n538\t    calibration_confusion_vs_scs_spearman: 0.32\n539\t  result_rationale: 'SDGD-cal 相比 SDGD-zero 提升 ~1.5pp，原因是 empirical confusion 直接捕获\n540\t    模型特异的混淆模式（如 Qwen3 特别容易混淆 building-library ↔ building-hotel 但 embedding 距离中等的 pair），绕过了\n541\t    embedding proxy 的噪声。 但 +2.6pp vs single-pass 仍不显著（p≈0.09），因为： (1) 8 个 calibration\n542\t    examples 的 confusion matrix 高方差——很多 type pairs 在 8 个样本中从未共现，confusion 为 0 但真实\n543\t    confusability 非零； (2) 从 calibration 到 test set 的 confusion 分布偏移——calibration examples\n544\t    的 type 分布未必代表 test set； (3) context loss 问题仍在——SDGD-cal 只改善了 confusability graph\n545\t    的质量， 不改变 decomposition 本身的 context-loss tradeoff。 这个结果在 median 档下留出\"SDGD-cal 有空间\"的\n546\t    narrative—— 更多 calibration data 或更好的 calibration protocol 预期可以继续提升。\n547\t\n548\t    '\n549\t  tables:\n550\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD Variant Comparison on Few-NERD'\n551\t    content: '| Method      | F1    | ΔF1 vs SP | Type Confusion ↓ | API Calls |\n552\t\n553\t      |-------------|-------|-----------|------------------|-----------|\n554\t\n555\t      | Single-pass | 0.414 | —         | —                | 1         |\n556\t\n557\t      | SDGD-zero   | 0.425 | +1.1      | -24%             | 8         |\n558\t\n559\t      | SDGD-cal    | 0.440 | +2.6      | -35%             | 536       |\n560\t\n561\t      '\n562\t  figures_description:\n563\t  - 'Line chart: F1 improvement trajectory from single-pass → SDGD-zero → SDGD-cal,\n564\t    with error bars. Upward trend but CIs overlap.'\n565\t  - 'Confusion matrix diff: empirical (calibration) vs embedding-predicted, highlighting\n566\t    discrepancies.'\n567\t  analysis: 'SDGD-cal 展示 confusability-aware decomposition 的 ceiling 更高， 但 8-example\n568\t    calibration 尚不足以稳定地达到。论文可报告为\"SDGD-cal 提供方向， 充分 calibration 数据下预期更大收益，但当前 training-free\n569\t    设定下的 calibration 成本 与收益比尚需优化\"。作为 SDGD-cal 的存在证明而非 headline 结果。\n570\t\n571\t    '\n572\t- name: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n573\t  plan_id: exp-011\n574\t  description: 'SDGD-cal 在 MAVEN 168 event types 上运行。 测试 empirical confusion 能否克服\n575\t    MAVEN 上 embedding proxy 失效的问题。\n576\t\n577\t    '\n578\t  expected_results:\n579\t    sdgd_cal_relaxed_f1: 0.258\n580\t    sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.24\n581\t    singlepass_relaxed_f1: 0.245\n582\t    delta_cal_vs_singlepass_pp: 1.3\n583\t    delta_cal_vs_zero_pp: 1.8\n584\t    significant: false\n585\t    calibration_api_calls: 1344\n586\t    total_api_calls: 1358\n587\t  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 收益更大（+1.8pp vs +0.5pp on Few-NERD），\n588\t    因为 MAVEN 正是 embedding proxy 失效的数据集（Qwen3 pairwise r=-0.007）。 Empirical confusion\n589\t    绕过了 embedding 的限制，直接用模型行为构建 graph。 但绝对增益仍有限（+1.3pp vs single-pass），因为： (1) 168\n590\t    types 的 calibration matrix 极其稀疏——168×167/2=14028 pairs 中， 8 个 calibration samples\n591\t    能覆盖的 pair 比例很低； (2) MAVEN 的 exact F1 极低，relaxed F1 的 variance 大，信噪比低； (3) 1344\n592\t    API calls 的 calibration 成本在实用性上存疑。 这支持了\"SDGD-cal 在 embedding 失效场景下价值更大\"的论点， 也说明了\"calibration\n593\t    效率是未来工作方向\"。\n594\t\n595\t    '\n596\t  tables:\n597\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines on MAVEN'\n598\t    content: '| Method      | Relaxed F1 | Δ vs SP  | API Calls |\n599\t\n600\t      |-------------|-----------|----------|-----------|\n601\t\n602\t      | Single-pass | 0.245     | —        | 1         |\n603\t\n604\t      | SDGD-zero   | 0.240     | -0.5     | 14        |\n605\t\n606\t      | SDGD-cal    | 0.258     | +1.3     | 1358      |\n607\t\n608\t      '\n609\t  figures_description:\n610\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: SDGD-zero vs SDGD-cal improvement over single-pass, Few-NERD\n611\t    vs MAVEN. MAVEN shows larger cal-zero gap.'\n612\t  analysis: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal > SDGD-zero 的差距（1.8pp）大于 Few-NERD（1.5pp）， 验证了\"当 embedding\n613\t    proxy 失效时 empirical calibration 价值更高\"的预测。 但绝对增益仍不显著，reinforces median-tier narrative。\n614\t\n615\t    '\n616\t- name: Random Batching Ablation\n617\t  plan_id: exp-013\n618\t  description: 'Random batching（与 SDGD 同 k，随机分组）ablation。 隔离 confusability-aware grouping\n619\t    的贡献 vs 纯 batch count reduction。\n620\t\n621\t    '\n622\t  expected_results:\n623\t    random_batching_f1: 0.418\n624\t    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n625\t    singlepass_f1: 0.414\n626\t    delta_sdgd_vs_random_pp: 0.7\n627\t    delta_random_vs_singlepass_pp: 0.4\n628\t    random_batching_recall: 0.325\n629\t    random_batching_precision: 0.565\n630\t    type_confusion_errors:\n631\t      random: 2150\n632\t      sdgd_zero: 1850\n633\t      singlepass: 2434\n634\t    n_random_seeds: 5\n635\t    f1_std_across_seeds: 0.018\n636\t  result_rationale: 'Random batching vs single-pass 仅 +0.4pp——count reduction 本身的收益很小，\n637\t    因为 Few-NERD 66 types 分成 8 batches of ~8 types，每个 batch 仍然有足够的 type diversity 来产生\n638\t    confusion。Random batching 的 confusion rate 高于 SDGD-zero 但低于 single-pass，因为随机分组偶然也会分开一些\n639\t    confusable pairs。 SDGD-zero vs random 的差异（+0.7pp）代表了 confusability-aware grouping\n640\t    的 增量贡献——统计上不显著但方向一致，5 seeds 的 F1 std=0.018 反映分组方案敏感性。 这个结果在 median 档下支持\"SDGD 的\n641\t    confusability-aware grouping 有正面方向 但需要更好的 confusability 信号（如 SDGD-cal）才能变得显著\"的叙事。\n642\t\n643\t    '\n644\t  tables:\n645\t  - name: 'Table: Batching Strategy Ablation (Few-NERD, k=8)'\n646\t    content: '| Strategy     | F1    | Recall | Prec  | TypeConfusion | Seeds |\n647\t\n648\t      |-------------|-------|--------|-------|---------------|-------|\n649\t\n650\t      | Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.304  | 0.648 | 2434          | 1     |\n651\t\n652\t      | Random      | 0.418 | 0.325  | 0.565 | 2150          | 5     |\n653\t\n654\t      | SDGD-zero   | 0.425 | 0.335  | 0.580 | 1850          | 1     |\n655\t\n656\t      '\n657\t  figures_description:\n658\t  - 'Box plot: 5 random seeds'' F1 distribution vs SDGD-zero (single point), SDGD-zero\n659\t    at or near upper end of random distribution.'\n660\t  analysis: 'SDGD-zero 位于 random batching 分布的上端但未显著超出—— 这意味着 confusability-aware grouping\n661\t    有 signal 但 magnitude 有限。 报告为\"SDGD directionality confirmed, magnitude requires\n662\t    stronger confusability signal\"。\n663\t\n664\t    '\n665\t- name: Per-type Splitting (UniNER-style) Ablation\n666\t  plan_id: exp-014\n667\t  description: '每个 type 一个 batch（k=66），UniNER 风格。 消融 decomposition 的上界和 cross-type\n668\t    context loss 效应。\n669\t\n670\t    '\n671\t  expected_results:\n672\t    per_type_f1: 0.395\n673\t    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n674\t    singlepass_f1: 0.414\n675\t    delta_per_type_vs_singlepass_pp: -1.9\n676\t    delta_per_type_vs_sdgd_pp: -3.0\n677\t    per_type_recall: 0.385\n678\t    per_type_precision: 0.405\n679\t    api_calls: 66\n680\t    wall_clock_minutes: 45\n681\t    sdgd_wall_clock_minutes: 12\n682\t    singlepass_wall_clock_minutes: 4\n683\t    type_confusion_errors: 0\n684\t    omission_errors: 4500\n685\t  result_rationale: 'Per-type splitting 完全消除 type confusion（confusion=0，因为每 batch\n686\t    只有一个 type） 但代价巨大： (1) Cross-type context 完全丧失——模型无法通过排除其他类型来确认当前类型， 导致大量 false\n687\t    negatives（omission 4500 vs single-pass 2850）； (2) 每个 batch 的 type 描述缺乏对比上下文，模型倾向于\n688\t    over-predict（每个 batch 里任何看起来沾边的 span 都被标注），但因为只有一个 type 所以 precision 不高； (3) 66\n689\t    个 API calls 的延迟不可接受（45 min vs 4 min single-pass）； (4) F1=0.395 低于 single-pass\n690\t    和 SDGD-zero——这是\"过度分解\"的直接证据。 这个结果对论文至关重要：证明 naive decomposition (UniNER-style)\n691\t    不是答案， confusability-AWARE grouping（而非简单拆分）才是正确方向。\n692\t\n693\t    '\n694\t  tables:\n695\t  - name: 'Table: Decomposition Strategy Spectrum'\n696\t    content: '| Strategy     | k  | F1    | Confusion | Omission | Latency (min) |\n697\t\n698\t      |-------------|-----|-------|-----------|----------|---------------|\n699\t\n700\t      | Single-pass | 1   | 0.414 | 2434      | 2850     | 4             |\n701\t\n702\t      | SDGD-zero   | 8   | 0.425 | 1850      | 3200     | 12            |\n703\t\n704\t      | Random      | 8   | 0.418 | 2150      | 3100     | 12            |\n705\t\n706\t      | Per-type    | 66  | 0.395 | 0         | 4500     | 45            |\n707\t\n708\t      '\n709\t  figures_description:\n710\t  - 'Trade-off curve: F1 vs number of batches k, showing inverted-U peaking at k≈8-12.\n711\t    Per-type (k=66) falls off sharply.'\n712\t  - 'Stacked error bar: confusion + omission across strategies, showing the substitution↓/omission↑\n713\t    tradeoff spectrum.'\n714\t  analysis: 'Per-type splitting 是 decomposition spectrum 的极端端点，其 F1 下降证明 cross-type\n715\t    context 有正面价值——LLM 需要看到相关类型才能做出正确区分。 SDGD 的价值在于找到 optimal k 使得 confusability reduction\n716\t    和 context preservation 之间取得平衡。即使 SDGD-zero 增益不显著，它至少不损害性能（unlike per-type）， 这本身就是有意义的\n717\t    design insight。\n718\t\n719\t    '\n720\t- name: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Validation\n721\t  plan_id: exp-015\n722\t  description: 'Spearman/Kendall correlation between embedding SCS 和 calibration 实测\n723\t    confusion matrix。 验证 embedding proxy 的实用性上界。\n724\t\n725\t    '\n726\t  expected_results:\n727\t    fewnerd_qwen3:\n728\t      spearman_rho: 0.35\n729\t      kendall_tau: 0.25\n730\t      p_value: 2.0e-08\n731\t      n_pairs_with_confusion: 285\n732\t    fewnerd_minilm:\n733\t      spearman_rho: 0.22\n734\t      kendall_tau: 0.16\n735\t      p_value: 0.0003\n736\t      n_pairs_with_confusion: 285\n737\t    top10_overlap_qwen3: 0.5\n738\t    top10_overlap_minilm: 0.3\n739\t    rank_agreement_top50_qwen3: 0.42\n740\t  result_rationale: \"Embedding SCS 与 empirical confusion 的相关性中等（ρ≈0.35 for Qwen3），原因是：\\\n741\t    \\ (1) Embedding 相似性捕获了语义距离但 LLM confusion 还受到：\\n   - type name 的词汇重叠（\\\"person-artist\\\"\\\n742\t    \\ vs \\\"person-politician\\\" 共享前缀）\\n   - pretraining data 中类型的 co-occurrence 频率\\n\\\n743\t    \\   - prompt 格式对不同类型名的 tokenization 差异\\n这些因素不反映在 embedding SCS 中； (2) Qwen3 SCS\\\n744\t    \\ > MiniLM SCS（ρ=0.35 vs 0.22）因为 Qwen3 是 extraction model 本身的 embedding，更接近模型内部的\\\n745\t    \\ type representation； (3) Top-10 overlap 50%（Qwen3）意味着一半的最高混淆 pairs 被 embedding\\\n746\t    \\ 正确识别， 但另一半被遗漏——这解释了为什么 SDGD-zero 效果有限而 SDGD-cal 更好。 这个结果为 embedding 选择提供了 principled\\\n747\t    \\ guidance： 如果可以用 extraction model 自身的 embedding，优先使用；否则用 SDGD-cal。\\n\"\n748\t  tables:\n749\t  - name: 'Table: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Correlation'\n750\t    content: '| Embedding | Spearman ρ | Kendall τ | Top-10 Overlap | n pairs |\n751\t\n752\t      |-----------|-----------|-----------|----------------|---------|\n753\t\n754\t      | Qwen3     | 0.35      | 0.25      | 50%            | 285     |\n755\t\n756\t      | MiniLM    | 0.22      | 0.16      | 30%            | 285     |\n757\t\n758\t      '\n759\t  figures_description:\n760\t  - 'Scatter: Qwen3 SCS vs empirical confusion rate (log scale), with marginal histograms\n761\t    showing SCS concentration.'\n762\t  - 'Precision-at-k curve: fraction of top-k SCS pairs that are in top-k empirical\n763\t    confusion pairs, for k=5,10,20,50.'\n764\t  analysis: SCS 是 reasonable proxy（ρ=0.35, 显著）但远非 perfect predictor（ρ<0.5）。 这解释了 SDGD-zero\n765\t    与 SDGD-cal 的 performance gap，并为\"何时用哪种 SDGD 变体\" 提供了 decision criterion：embedding\n766\t    SCS 适合 quick-and-dirty decomposition， empirical calibration 适合 high-stakes applications。\n767\t    论文中作为 2×3 ablation 的 quantitative backing。\n768\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08912b4a-ab76-4663-b333-b897e4b7593f","uuid":"5791b11e-5cf1-4925-bddc-532b36bad320","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:26:00.845Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_18/projects/schema-dag-extraction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T113743/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '论文重心 80:20（分析:方法）。三层贡献：(1) pairwise confusability 跨 NER/RE/ED\n  三任务、Qwen3+LLaMA 双模型成立， (2) multi-channel degradation model（count→omission, confusability→substitution）+\n  错误分类学， (3) centrality confound 方法论发现 + 2×3 embedding ablation practitioner guidance。\n  SDGD-zero 保留为 proof-of-concept 但 ΔF1 不显著（[-2,+2]pp），Claim 3 改写为 \"SDGD 框架示范 pairwise\n  confusability 可直接指导 schema decomposition，SDGD-cal 预期有更大空间\"。 EMNLP Main 可冲（对标 Lost\n  in the Middle），Findings 作后备。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: MAVEN Full Confusability Study\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: 'MAVEN 168 event类型，count curve + within-count BCS correlation + pairwise/per-type分析。\n    跨任务验证（NER→ED），同域语义密集 schema 的 confusability 行为。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    count_curve_relaxed_f1:\n      count_1: 0.106\n      count_6: 0.103\n      count_12: 0.146\n      count_22: 0.185\n      count_44: 0.247\n      count_64: 0.245\n      count_168: 0.22\n    count_curve_exact_f1:\n      count_1: 0.009\n      count_6: 0.003\n      count_12: 0.008\n      count_22: 0.013\n      count_44: 0.018\n      count_64: 0.013\n    pairwise_minilm:\n      pearson_r: 0.115\n      pearson_p: 2.0e-34\n      n_pairs: 11026\n      spearman_rho: 0.098\n      spearman_p: 1.5e-24\n    pairwise_qwen3:\n      pearson_r: -0.007\n      pearson_p: 0.41\n      verdict: NOT_SIGNIFICANT\n    per_type_qwen3:\n      spearman_rho: 0.189\n      spearman_p: 0.021\n      direction: POSITIVE (centrality confound)\n    per_type_minilm:\n      spearman_rho: 0.208\n      spearman_p: 0.011\n      direction: POSITIVE (centrality confound)\n    within_count_bcs_relaxed_f1:\n      count_6_r: 0.12\n      count_6_p: 0.18\n      count_12_r: 0.09\n      count_12_p: 0.28\n      verdict: FAIL — batch-level BCS confounded by centrality\n    confusion_rate_ratio_extreme:\n      count_6: 7.5\n      count_12: 5.2\n  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 168 类型全部来自 FrameNet 同域层级，语义空间高度同质（scs_mean=0.216， scs_std=0.103），导致两个层面行为分离：\n    (1) Pairwise MiniLM 成立（r≈0.12）——因为 MiniLM 对细粒度事件类型对（如 Destroying↔Damaging） 的相对差异敏感，pair-level\n    分析不受聚合效应影响； (2) Pairwise Qwen3 不显著——Qwen3 extraction-aligned embedding 在同域 schema\n    中 将语义相近类型压缩到近乎相同的向量，丧失区分力； (3) Per-type 两种 embedding 均为正向 ρ≈+0.19/+0.21——这是 centrality\n    confound： 在同质 schema 中 mean BCS 高的类型恰好是语义中心、高频类型，LLM 对其提取效果好。 这不是分析失败，而是方法论贡献——识别出\"per-type\n    聚合在何时失效\"的具体机制。 Within-count batch-level 相关不显著，因为 batch-level BCS 范围被 schema 同质性压缩\n    （0.87-0.94），区分度不足。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: MAVEN Count Curve (Relaxed F1)'\n    content: '| Count | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | Recall | Precision |\n\n      |-------|-----------|----------|--------|-----------|\n\n      | 1     | 0.106     | 0.009    | 0.142  | 0.083     |\n\n      | 6     | 0.103     | 0.003    | 0.130  | 0.085     |\n\n      | 12    | 0.146     | 0.008    | 0.172  | 0.127     |\n\n      | 22    | 0.185     | 0.013    | 0.210  | 0.165     |\n\n      | 44    | 0.247     | 0.018    | 0.268  | 0.229     |\n\n      | 64    | 0.245     | 0.013    | 0.255  | 0.236     |\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table: MAVEN Pairwise & Per-type Analysis (2×2 Embedding Matrix)'\n    content: '| Level     | Qwen3          | MiniLM          |\n\n      |-----------|----------------|-----------------|\n\n      | Pairwise  | r=-0.007 (ns)  | r=+0.115 ✓      |\n\n      | Per-type  | ρ=+0.189 ✗     | ρ=+0.208 ✗      |\n\n      Note: ✓=supports confusability hypothesis, ✗=centrality confound direction\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: MiniLM pairwise SCS vs confusion count (11K pairs), with regression\n    line r=0.115. Long tail of high-SCS pairs with elevated confusion.'\n  - 'Bar chart: per-type mean BCS quartiles vs relaxed F1, showing positive trend\n    (centrality confound). Annotated with frequency distribution per quartile.'\n  - 'Heatmap: top-20 confused event type pairs, colored by MiniLM SCS. Diagonal stripe\n    pattern showing FrameNet siblings.'\n  analysis: 'MAVEN 为 pairwise confusability 提供跨任务复现（NER→ED），同时暴露 per-type 聚合的 centrality\n    confound 机制。MiniLM pairwise r=0.115 与 Few-NERD r=0.156 量级一致， 但 Qwen3 在同域 schema\n    上失效，证实\"embedding 选择影响信号检测\"的结论。 Per-type 正向 ρ 构成独立方法论贡献：当 schema 语义同质时，mean BCS\n    不再是 confusability 的有效聚合指标，需回退到 pairwise level。\n\n    '\n- name: DocRED Confusability Scaling Test\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 'DocRED 96 relation types，count curve + BCS correlation。 文档级 RE 的 scaling\n    stress test，验证 confusability 信号在更复杂抽取设置下是否成立。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    count_curve_f1:\n      count_1: 0.18\n      count_6: 0.22\n      count_12: 0.25\n      count_24: 0.23\n      count_48: 0.19\n      count_96: 0.14\n    pairwise_qwen3:\n      pearson_r: 0.082\n      pearson_p: 0.008\n      n_pairs: 4560\n    pairwise_minilm:\n      pearson_r: 0.095\n      pearson_p: 0.001\n    per_type_qwen3:\n      spearman_rho: -0.165\n      spearman_p: 0.108\n    within_count_bcs_f1:\n      count_12_r: 0.18\n      count_12_p: 0.12\n      count_24_r: 0.25\n      count_24_p: 0.065\n  result_rationale: 'DocRED 是文档级 RE，96 relation types 跨越多域（人物、地理、组织等）， 语义异质性介于 Few-NERD（跨域\n    NER）和 MAVEN（同域 ED）之间。 Pairwise 信号可检测（r≈0.08-0.10）但弱于 Few-NERD（r=0.156），原因是： (1)\n    文档级 RE 噪声更大——同一文档多个 relation 共现，confusion 来源更复杂； (2) relation type 的语义相似性比 entity\n    type 更抽象（\"country of citizenship\" vs \"place of birth\" 的 embedding 距离不完全反映 LLM\n    的实际混淆模式）； (3) DocRED 的 distant supervision 标注本身有噪声，增加 metric variance。 Per-type\n    方向一致（负 ρ）但因 n=96 types + 噪声，未达显著。 作为 P1 实验，主要贡献是\"第四个数据点\"但非必须——三任务已足够。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: DocRED Count Curve'\n    content: '| Count | F1    | Recall | Precision |\n\n      |-------|-------|--------|-----------|\n\n      | 1     | 0.180 | 0.280  | 0.133     |\n\n      | 6     | 0.220 | 0.290  | 0.178     |\n\n      | 12    | 0.250 | 0.275  | 0.229     |\n\n      | 24    | 0.230 | 0.240  | 0.221     |\n\n      | 48    | 0.190 | 0.195  | 0.185     |\n\n      | 96    | 0.140 | 0.135  | 0.146     |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - DocRED count curve overlay with Few-NERD (normalized F1), showing both exhibit\n    inverted-U but DocRED peaks earlier (count_12 vs count_44).\n  analysis: 'DocRED 提供第四个数据点但效应量衰减。如果时间紧张（ARR deadline 10 天）， 可降级为 appendix 或完全跳过——Few-NERD\n    + FewRel + MAVEN 已覆盖 NER/RE/ED 三任务。\n\n    '\n- name: Count × Confusability Interaction Effect\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: '2×2 factorial：{low count (6), high count (22)} × {low BCS, high BCS}，Few-NERD。\n    检验 count 和 confusability 的交互是加性还是乘性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    cell_f1:\n      low_count_low_bcs: 0.355\n      low_count_high_bcs: 0.305\n      high_count_low_bcs: 0.295\n      high_count_high_bcs: 0.23\n    main_effect_count:\n      delta_f1_pp: -6.3\n      f_stat: 8.2\n      p_value: 0.007\n    main_effect_bcs:\n      delta_f1_pp: -5.8\n      f_stat: 6.5\n      p_value: 0.015\n    interaction:\n      f_stat: 1.4\n      p_value: 0.24\n      effect_size_eta2: 0.03\n    model_comparison:\n      additive_R2: 0.38\n      multiplicative_R2: 0.39\n  result_rationale: 'Count 和 confusability 通过不同通道降解性能：count 导致 recall 下降（omission），\n    confusability 导致 precision 下降（substitution）。这两个通道大致正交—— 增加 count 不会显著放大 confusability\n    的效应，反之亦然。 Interaction term 不显著（p≈0.24）的原因是：(1) 两通道作用于不同错误类型， 物理上近似独立；(2) 2×2 设计只有\n    ~20 batches/cell，检测交互效应的统计功效有限。 Additive model 已解释 ~38% 方差，interaction 仅贡献 1%。\n    这实际上支持 multi-channel model 的核心主张——count 和 confusability 可独立处理。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: 2×2 Factorial Results'\n    content: '|                | Low BCS  | High BCS | Marginal |\n\n      |----------------|----------|----------|----------|\n\n      | Low count (6)  | 0.355    | 0.305    | 0.330    |\n\n      | High count (22)| 0.295    | 0.230    | 0.263    |\n\n      | Marginal       | 0.325    | 0.268    |          |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Interaction plot: two roughly parallel lines (low BCS, high BCS) across count\n    levels, illustrating additive (not synergistic) effect.'\n  analysis: '加性模型优于乘性模型但 margin 很小。关键 takeaway 是\"two independent knobs\"—— 从业者可以分别优化\n    batch size（控制 count 通道）和 batch composition（控制 confusability 通道）， 无需考虑复杂交互。这是 practitioner\n    guidance 的基础。\n\n    '\n- name: Systematic Error Taxonomy\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: '跨 BCS bins 的 FP 系统分类：type_substitution / boundary_error / omission\n    / hallucination。 为 multi-channel model 提供机制证据。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    error_distribution_high_bcs:\n      type_substitution_pct: 62\n      boundary_error_pct: 14\n      omission_pct: 18\n      hallucination_pct: 6\n    error_distribution_low_bcs:\n      type_substitution_pct: 28\n      boundary_error_pct: 22\n      omission_pct: 42\n      hallucination_pct: 8\n    error_distribution_medium_bcs:\n      type_substitution_pct: 45\n      boundary_error_pct: 18\n      omission_pct: 30\n      hallucination_pct: 7\n    substitution_ratio_high_vs_low: 2.2\n    omission_ratio_low_vs_high: 2.3\n    substitution_trend_with_count:\n      count_6: 0.35\n      count_12: 0.48\n      count_22: 0.55\n    omission_trend_with_count:\n      count_6: 0.28\n      count_12: 0.32\n      count_22: 0.38\n  result_rationale: 'Error taxonomy 是 multi-channel model 的直接机制验证。 High-BCS batches\n    中 type_substitution 占主导（~62%）因为语义相似类型共现时 LLM 识别了正确的 span 但选错了类型标签——这正是 confusability\n    channel 的定义。 Low-BCS batches 中 omission 占主导（~42%）因为虽然类型不相似但数量多， LLM 的 attention\n    被分散，更多实体被完全遗漏——这是 count channel。 Substitution 随 count 增加（0.35→0.55）因为更多类型意味着更多潜在混淆对。\n    Omission 也随 count 增加（0.28→0.38）因为 attention dilution 加剧。 两种错误都对 count 有响应，但 confusability\n    只放大 substitution，不影响 omission—— 这是两通道正交性的直接证据。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Error Distribution by BCS Bin'\n    content: '| Error Type       | Low BCS | Med BCS | High BCS |\n\n      |------------------|---------|---------|----------|\n\n      | Type Substitution| 28%     | 45%     | 62%      |\n\n      | Boundary Error   | 22%     | 18%     | 14%      |\n\n      | Omission         | 42%     | 30%     | 18%      |\n\n      | Hallucination    | 8%      | 7%      | 6%       |\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table: Error Rates by Count Level (All BCS)'\n    content: '| Error Type       | Count 6 | Count 12 | Count 22 |\n\n      |------------------|---------|----------|----------|\n\n      | Substitution Rate| 0.035   | 0.048    | 0.055    |\n\n      | Omission Rate    | 0.028   | 0.032    | 0.038    |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Stacked bar chart: error type composition across 5 BCS quintiles, showing substitution/omission\n    crossover at BCS≈0.82.'\n  - 'Dual-axis line chart: substitution rate (left axis) and omission rate (right\n    axis) vs count, both increasing but substitution steeper.'\n  analysis: 'Error taxonomy 将 \"confusability degrades extraction\" 的抽象主张具象化为可操作的诊断框架：\n    看到 high substitution rate → confusability 问题 → SDGD-style decomposition； 看到 high\n    omission rate → count 问题 → reduce batch size。 这本身是论文的独立贡献，特别是在 Claim 3 (SDGD gains)\n    不显著的 median 档下， 错误分类学提供了\"分析即贡献\"的具体证据。\n\n    '\n- name: LLaMA-3.3-70B Multi-Model Validation\n  plan_id: exp-012\n  description: 'LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 复现 exp-002 协议。 验证 confusability 信号的模型无关性——是\n    schema 属性而非模型特异行为。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    fewnerd_pairwise:\n      pearson_r: 0.098\n      pearson_p: 3.2e-05\n      n_pairs: 1953\n      spearman_rho: 0.105\n      spearman_p: 8.7e-06\n      nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.195\n      nonzero_spearman_p: 0.0004\n    fewnerd_per_type:\n      spearman_rho: -0.215\n      spearman_p: 0.089\n      partial_r_ctrl_logfreq: -0.155\n      partial_p: 0.225\n    count_curve_f1:\n      count_1: 0.285\n      count_6: 0.27\n      count_12: 0.305\n      count_22: 0.265\n      count_44: 0.38\n      count_64: 0.355\n    confusion_rate_ratio_extreme:\n      count_6: 12.5\n      count_12: 6.8\n    batch_level_f1_vs_bcs:\n      count_12_r: 0.38\n      count_12_p: 0.045\n  result_rationale: 'LLaMA-3.3-70B 复现 pairwise 信号（r≈0.10, p<0.001）但效应量小于 Qwen3（r=0.156），\n    原因是： (1) LLaMA 和 Qwen3 架构不同（LLaMA 使用 GQA vs Qwen3 使用 GQA+SWA）， 对 prompt 中类型列表的\n    attention 分配模式不同，导致 confusability 的表现形式有差异； (2) LLaMA-70B 参数量更大（70B vs 32B），可能对\n    confusable types 有更强的区分能力， 从而压缩效应量； (3) 但 pairwise 信号方向一致且显著——confusability 是\n    schema 结构属性， 不同模型都会受影响，只是程度不同。 Per-type ρ=-0.215 方向一致但 p=0.089 未达 0.05——这在 median\n    档预期范围内 （cross_model_significant: [1,2]），pairwise 显著已足够支撑 multi-model claim。 Overall\n    F1 水平比 Qwen3 低 5-10%，可能因 LLaMA 的 NER few-shot 能力略弱。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-Model Pairwise Comparison'\n    content: '| Metric              | Qwen3-32B   | LLaMA-3.3-70B |\n\n      |---------------------|-------------|---------------|\n\n      | Pairwise r          | 0.156       | 0.098         |\n\n      | Pairwise p          | 4.6e-12     | 3.2e-05       |\n\n      | Per-type ρ          | -0.293*     | -0.215        |\n\n      | Confusion ratio (6) | 27.5x       | 12.5x         |\n\n      | Confusion ratio (12)| 9.9x        | 6.8x          |\n\n      * p<0.05\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table: LLaMA Count Curve'\n    content: '| Count | F1    | Recall | Precision |\n\n      |-------|-------|--------|-----------|\n\n      | 1     | 0.285 | 0.580  | 0.190     |\n\n      | 6     | 0.270 | 0.420  | 0.200     |\n\n      | 12    | 0.305 | 0.310  | 0.300     |\n\n      | 22    | 0.265 | 0.255  | 0.275     |\n\n      | 44    | 0.380 | 0.365  | 0.396     |\n\n      | 64    | 0.355 | 0.280  | 0.485     |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Overlay scatter: Qwen3 vs LLaMA pairwise SCS-confusion, same axes. Both positive\n    slopes, LLaMA shallower.'\n  - 'Side-by-side confusion heatmaps (top-20 pairs): substantial overlap in confused\n    pairs between models.'\n  analysis: 'LLaMA 在 pairwise level 显著复现信号（r≥0.08, p<0.05），满足 median 档 cross_model_significant\n    ≥1 的阈值。Per-type 未达显著但方向一致。 效应量差异本身是有意义的发现——更大的模型可能对 confusability 更鲁棒， 暗示 confusability\n    降解是 training-free setting 的固有挑战，可通过 scaling 部分缓解但不消除。 论文中报告为\"cross-model replication\n    with attenuated but significant effect\"。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: 'Confusability-minimizing batch composition：embedding SCS 阈值化 → confusability\n    graph → graph coloring → batches。对比 single-pass full-schema baseline。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    sdgd_zero_config:\n      embedding: qwen3\n      threshold: 0.85\n      n_batches: 8\n      avg_batch_size: 8.25\n      coloring_algorithm: greedy_dsatur\n    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n    singlepass_f1: 0.414\n    delta_f1_pp: 1.1\n    delta_f1_ci_95:\n    - -1.5\n    - 3.7\n    p_value_paired_t: 0.18\n    significant: false\n    sdgd_zero_recall: 0.335\n    sdgd_zero_precision: 0.58\n    singlepass_recall: 0.304\n    singlepass_precision: 0.648\n    type_confusion_errors:\n      sdgd_zero: 1850\n      singlepass: 2434\n      reduction_pct: 24\n    omission_errors:\n      sdgd_zero: 3200\n      singlepass: 2850\n      increase_pct: 12\n    api_calls: 8\n    wall_clock_ratio: 3.2\n  result_rationale: 'SDGD-zero 在 median 档下 ΔF1≈+1.1pp，置信区间跨零，不显著。核心权衡： (1) Confusability\n    降低的收益——分离 confusable types（如 person-other 和 person-politician 不再共现于同一 batch），type\n    confusion errors 减少 ~24%，precision 改善； (2) 跨类型上下文丢失的代价——单 batch 只看到 ~8 个类型而非全部\n    66 个， LLM 无法利用\"这不是 X 所以应该是 Y\"的排除推理，omission errors 增加 ~12%； (3) 这两个效应在 F1 层面大致抵消。Precision\n    提升（0.648→0.580 actually下降... 不对，让我修正）——SDGD-zero 的 recall 高于 single-pass（0.335>0.304）因为\n    smaller batches 意味着更少的 attention dilution，但 precision 降低因为 smaller batches 使模型缺少同\n    batch 内的对比信号。 净效应：recall 提升 + precision 下降 → F1 微小提升但不显著。 这正是 median 档的核心判断——decomposition\n    是可行的框架但不是 silver bullet。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SDGD-zero vs Single-pass on Few-NERD (66 types)'\n    content: '| Method      | F1    | Recall | Precision | Type Confusion | Omission\n      | API Calls |\n\n      |-------------|-------|--------|-----------|----------------|----------|-----------|\n\n      | Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.304  | 0.648     | 2434           | 2850     | 1         |\n\n      | SDGD-zero   | 0.425 | 0.335  | 0.580     | 1850           | 3200     | 8         |\n\n      | Δ           | +1.1  | +3.1   | -6.8      | -24%           | +12%     | +7        |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired bar chart: error type breakdown for single-pass vs SDGD-zero, showing\n    substitution↓ / omission↑ tradeoff.'\n  - 'Scatter: per-batch F1 vs batch mean BCS for SDGD-zero batches, showing SDGD batches\n    cluster at low BCS.'\n  analysis: 'SDGD-zero 的价值不在于 F1 增益（不显著），而在于： (1) 验证 pairwise confusability 可直接转化为\n    actionable decomposition； (2) 错误 profile 的定向转移证实 multi-channel model——confusability\n    channel 可关闭（减 24% substitution）， 但代价是轻度激活 count channel（增 12% omission）； (3) 为\n    SDGD-cal 提供 baseline——如果用 empirical confusion 替代 embedding proxy， graph 更准确，预期收益更大。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: 'SDGD-zero 在 MAVEN 168 event types 上的跨任务验证。 同域高密度 schema 对 graph coloring\n    的挑战。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    sdgd_zero_config:\n      embedding: minilm\n      threshold: 0.35\n      n_batches: 14\n      avg_batch_size: 12\n    sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.24\n    singlepass_relaxed_f1: 0.245\n    random_batching_relaxed_f1: 0.235\n    delta_vs_singlepass_pp: -0.5\n    delta_vs_random_pp: 0.5\n    significant: false\n    sdgd_zero_exact_f1: 0.015\n    singlepass_exact_f1: 0.013\n    api_calls: 14\n  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 的同域同质 schema 对 SDGD-zero 极具挑战： (1) SCS 分布集中（mean=0.216,\n    std=0.103），大部分 pair 相似度在 0.1-0.35 范围， 用阈值 0.35 切分后 confusability graph 边数较少，graph\n    coloring 产生的 batches 与 random batching 差异不大； (2) 即使成功分离了高 SCS pairs（119 pairs\n    > 0.5），这些 pairs 分布在 168 个 types 中仅占 0.85%，对整体 F1 影响微小； (3) Exact F1 极低（<0.02）使得任何方法差异都淹没在\n    boundary matching 噪声中， relaxed F1 是唯一可比指标； (4) SDGD-zero 微弱优于 random batching（+0.5pp），但不优于\n    single-pass（-0.5pp）， 因为 MAVEN 的 context 更重要——event detection 依赖同一句中多种事件类型的对比。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SDGD-zero vs Baselines on MAVEN (168 types)'\n    content: '| Method          | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | API Calls |\n\n      |-----------------|-----------|----------|-----------|\n\n      | Single-pass     | 0.245     | 0.013    | 1         |\n\n      | Random (k=14)   | 0.235     | 0.012    | 14        |\n\n      | SDGD-zero       | 0.240     | 0.015    | 14        |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'MAVEN confusability graph visualization: near-complete subgraph structure, illustrating\n    why graph coloring fails to find clean separations.'\n  analysis: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-zero ≈ single-pass 进一步支持 median 档叙事： SDGD 是正确的框架但 -zero\n    变体在高密度 schema 上能力有限。 这也解释了为什么 embedding-based proxy 不够——需要 empirical confusion\n    data (SDGD-cal) 才能在同域 schema 上有效操作。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: '用 5-10 calibration examples 的 empirical confusion matrix 替代 embedding\n    SCS 构建 confusability graph。 检验 calibration 数据能否弥补 embedding proxy 的不足。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    calibration_config:\n      n_calibration_examples: 8\n      calibration_api_calls: 528\n      total_api_calls: 536\n    sdgd_cal_f1: 0.44\n    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n    singlepass_f1: 0.414\n    delta_cal_vs_zero_pp: 1.5\n    delta_cal_vs_singlepass_pp: 2.6\n    delta_cal_vs_singlepass_ci_95:\n    - -0.8\n    - 6.0\n    p_value_vs_singlepass: 0.09\n    significant_vs_singlepass: false\n    type_confusion_reduction_vs_singlepass_pct: 35\n    calibration_confusion_vs_scs_spearman: 0.32\n  result_rationale: 'SDGD-cal 相比 SDGD-zero 提升 ~1.5pp，原因是 empirical confusion 直接捕获\n    模型特异的混淆模式（如 Qwen3 特别容易混淆 building-library ↔ building-hotel 但 embedding 距离中等的 pair），绕过了\n    embedding proxy 的噪声。 但 +2.6pp vs single-pass 仍不显著（p≈0.09），因为： (1) 8 个 calibration\n    examples 的 confusion matrix 高方差——很多 type pairs 在 8 个样本中从未共现，confusion 为 0 但真实\n    confusability 非零； (2) 从 calibration 到 test set 的 confusion 分布偏移——calibration examples\n    的 type 分布未必代表 test set； (3) context loss 问题仍在——SDGD-cal 只改善了 confusability graph\n    的质量， 不改变 decomposition 本身的 context-loss tradeoff。 这个结果在 median 档下留出\"SDGD-cal 有空间\"的\n    narrative—— 更多 calibration data 或更好的 calibration protocol 预期可以继续提升。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SDGD Variant Comparison on Few-NERD'\n    content: '| Method      | F1    | ΔF1 vs SP | Type Confusion ↓ | API Calls |\n\n      |-------------|-------|-----------|------------------|-----------|\n\n      | Single-pass | 0.414 | —         | —                | 1         |\n\n      | SDGD-zero   | 0.425 | +1.1      | -24%             | 8         |\n\n      | SDGD-cal    | 0.440 | +2.6      | -35%             | 536       |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line chart: F1 improvement trajectory from single-pass → SDGD-zero → SDGD-cal,\n    with error bars. Upward trend but CIs overlap.'\n  - 'Confusion matrix diff: empirical (calibration) vs embedding-predicted, highlighting\n    discrepancies.'\n  analysis: 'SDGD-cal 展示 confusability-aware decomposition 的 ceiling 更高， 但 8-example\n    calibration 尚不足以稳定地达到。论文可报告为\"SDGD-cal 提供方向， 充分 calibration 数据下预期更大收益，但当前 training-free\n    设定下的 calibration 成本 与收益比尚需优化\"。作为 SDGD-cal 的存在证明而非 headline 结果。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: 'SDGD-cal 在 MAVEN 168 event types 上运行。 测试 empirical confusion 能否克服\n    MAVEN 上 embedding proxy 失效的问题。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    sdgd_cal_relaxed_f1: 0.258\n    sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.24\n    singlepass_relaxed_f1: 0.245\n    delta_cal_vs_singlepass_pp: 1.3\n    delta_cal_vs_zero_pp: 1.8\n    significant: false\n    calibration_api_calls: 1344\n    total_api_calls: 1358\n  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 收益更大（+1.8pp vs +0.5pp on Few-NERD），\n    因为 MAVEN 正是 embedding proxy 失效的数据集（Qwen3 pairwise r=-0.007）。 Empirical confusion\n    绕过了 embedding 的限制，直接用模型行为构建 graph。 但绝对增益仍有限（+1.3pp vs single-pass），因为： (1) 168\n    types 的 calibration matrix 极其稀疏——168×167/2=14028 pairs 中， 8 个 calibration samples\n    能覆盖的 pair 比例很低； (2) MAVEN 的 exact F1 极低，relaxed F1 的 variance 大，信噪比低； (3) 1344\n    API calls 的 calibration 成本在实用性上存疑。 这支持了\"SDGD-cal 在 embedding 失效场景下价值更大\"的论点， 也说明了\"calibration\n    效率是未来工作方向\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines on MAVEN'\n    content: '| Method      | Relaxed F1 | Δ vs SP  | API Calls |\n\n      |-------------|-----------|----------|-----------|\n\n      | Single-pass | 0.245     | —        | 1         |\n\n      | SDGD-zero   | 0.240     | -0.5     | 14        |\n\n      | SDGD-cal    | 0.258     | +1.3     | 1358      |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: SDGD-zero vs SDGD-cal improvement over single-pass, Few-NERD\n    vs MAVEN. MAVEN shows larger cal-zero gap.'\n  analysis: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal > SDGD-zero 的差距（1.8pp）大于 Few-NERD（1.5pp）， 验证了\"当 embedding\n    proxy 失效时 empirical calibration 价值更高\"的预测。 但绝对增益仍不显著，reinforces median-tier narrative。\n\n    '\n- name: Random Batching Ablation\n  plan_id: exp-013\n  description: 'Random batching（与 SDGD 同 k，随机分组）ablation。 隔离 confusability-aware grouping\n    的贡献 vs 纯 batch count reduction。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    random_batching_f1: 0.418\n    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n    singlepass_f1: 0.414\n    delta_sdgd_vs_random_pp: 0.7\n    delta_random_vs_singlepass_pp: 0.4\n    random_batching_recall: 0.325\n    random_batching_precision: 0.565\n    type_confusion_errors:\n      random: 2150\n      sdgd_zero: 1850\n      singlepass: 2434\n    n_random_seeds: 5\n    f1_std_across_seeds: 0.018\n  result_rationale: 'Random batching vs single-pass 仅 +0.4pp——count reduction 本身的收益很小，\n    因为 Few-NERD 66 types 分成 8 batches of ~8 types，每个 batch 仍然有足够的 type diversity 来产生\n    confusion。Random batching 的 confusion rate 高于 SDGD-zero 但低于 single-pass，因为随机分组偶然也会分开一些\n    confusable pairs。 SDGD-zero vs random 的差异（+0.7pp）代表了 confusability-aware grouping\n    的 增量贡献——统计上不显著但方向一致，5 seeds 的 F1 std=0.018 反映分组方案敏感性。 这个结果在 median 档下支持\"SDGD 的\n    confusability-aware grouping 有正面方向 但需要更好的 confusability 信号（如 SDGD-cal）才能变得显著\"的叙事。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Batching Strategy Ablation (Few-NERD, k=8)'\n    content: '| Strategy     | F1    | Recall | Prec  | TypeConfusion | Seeds |\n\n      |-------------|-------|--------|-------|---------------|-------|\n\n      | Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.304  | 0.648 | 2434          | 1     |\n\n      | Random      | 0.418 | 0.325  | 0.565 | 2150          | 5     |\n\n      | SDGD-zero   | 0.425 | 0.335  | 0.580 | 1850          | 1     |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Box plot: 5 random seeds'' F1 distribution vs SDGD-zero (single point), SDGD-zero\n    at or near upper end of random distribution.'\n  analysis: 'SDGD-zero 位于 random batching 分布的上端但未显著超出—— 这意味着 confusability-aware grouping\n    有 signal 但 magnitude 有限。 报告为\"SDGD directionality confirmed, magnitude requires\n    stronger confusability signal\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Per-type Splitting (UniNER-style) Ablation\n  plan_id: exp-014\n  description: '每个 type 一个 batch（k=66），UniNER 风格。 消融 decomposition 的上界和 cross-type\n    context loss 效应。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    per_type_f1: 0.395\n    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n    singlepass_f1: 0.414\n    delta_per_type_vs_singlepass_pp: -1.9\n    delta_per_type_vs_sdgd_pp: -3.0\n    per_type_recall: 0.385\n    per_type_precision: 0.405\n    api_calls: 66\n    wall_clock_minutes: 45\n    sdgd_wall_clock_minutes: 12\n    singlepass_wall_clock_minutes: 4\n    type_confusion_errors: 0\n    omission_errors: 4500\n  result_rationale: 'Per-type splitting 完全消除 type confusion（confusion=0，因为每 batch\n    只有一个 type） 但代价巨大： (1) Cross-type context 完全丧失——模型无法通过排除其他类型来确认当前类型， 导致大量 false\n    negatives（omission 4500 vs single-pass 2850）； (2) 每个 batch 的 type 描述缺乏对比上下文，模型倾向于\n    over-predict（每个 batch 里任何看起来沾边的 span 都被标注），但因为只有一个 type 所以 precision 不高； (3) 66\n    个 API calls 的延迟不可接受（45 min vs 4 min single-pass）； (4) F1=0.395 低于 single-pass\n    和 SDGD-zero——这是\"过度分解\"的直接证据。 这个结果对论文至关重要：证明 naive decomposition (UniNER-style)\n    不是答案， confusability-AWARE grouping（而非简单拆分）才是正确方向。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Decomposition Strategy Spectrum'\n    content: '| Strategy     | k  | F1    | Confusion | Omission | Latency (min) |\n\n      |-------------|-----|-------|-----------|----------|---------------|\n\n      | Single-pass | 1   | 0.414 | 2434      | 2850     | 4             |\n\n      | SDGD-zero   | 8   | 0.425 | 1850      | 3200     | 12            |\n\n      | Random      | 8   | 0.418 | 2150      | 3100     | 12            |\n\n      | Per-type    | 66  | 0.395 | 0         | 4500     | 45            |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Trade-off curve: F1 vs number of batches k, showing inverted-U peaking at k≈8-12.\n    Per-type (k=66) falls off sharply.'\n  - 'Stacked error bar: confusion + omission across strategies, showing the substitution↓/omission↑\n    tradeoff spectrum.'\n  analysis: 'Per-type splitting 是 decomposition spectrum 的极端端点，其 F1 下降证明 cross-type\n    context 有正面价值——LLM 需要看到相关类型才能做出正确区分。 SDGD 的价值在于找到 optimal k 使得 confusability reduction\n    和 context preservation 之间取得平衡。即使 SDGD-zero 增益不显著，它至少不损害性能（unlike per-type）， 这本身就是有意义的\n    design insight。\n\n    '\n- name: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Validation\n  plan_id: exp-015\n  description: 'Spearman/Kendall correlation between embedding SCS 和 calibration 实测\n    confusion matrix。 验证 embedding proxy 的实用性上界。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    fewnerd_qwen3:\n      spearman_rho: 0.35\n      kendall_tau: 0.25\n      p_value: 2.0e-08\n      n_pairs_with_confusion: 285\n    fewnerd_minilm:\n      spearman_rho: 0.22\n      kendall_tau: 0.16\n      p_value: 0.0003\n      n_pairs_with_confusion: 285\n    top10_overlap_qwen3: 0.5\n    top10_overlap_minilm: 0.3\n    rank_agreement_top50_qwen3: 0.42\n  result_rationale: \"Embedding SCS 与 empirical confusion 的相关性中等（ρ≈0.35 for Qwen3），原因是：\\\n    \\ (1) Embedding 相似性捕获了语义距离但 LLM confusion 还受到：\\n   - type name 的词汇重叠（\\\"person-artist\\\"\\\n    \\ vs \\\"person-politician\\\" 共享前缀）\\n   - pretraining data 中类型的 co-occurrence 频率\\n\\\n    \\   - prompt 格式对不同类型名的 tokenization 差异\\n这些因素不反映在 embedding SCS 中； (2) Qwen3 SCS\\\n    \\ > MiniLM SCS（ρ=0.35 vs 0.22）因为 Qwen3 是 extraction model 本身的 embedding，更接近模型内部的\\\n    \\ type representation； (3) Top-10 overlap 50%（Qwen3）意味着一半的最高混淆 pairs 被 embedding\\\n    \\ 正确识别， 但另一半被遗漏——这解释了为什么 SDGD-zero 效果有限而 SDGD-cal 更好。 这个结果为 embedding 选择提供了 principled\\\n    \\ guidance： 如果可以用 extraction model 自身的 embedding，优先使用；否则用 SDGD-cal。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Correlation'\n    content: '| Embedding | Spearman ρ | Kendall τ | Top-10 Overlap | n pairs |\n\n      |-----------|-----------|-----------|----------------|---------|\n\n      | Qwen3     | 0.35      | 0.25      | 50%            | 285     |\n\n      | MiniLM    | 0.22      | 0.16      | 30%            | 285     |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter: Qwen3 SCS vs empirical confusion rate (log scale), with marginal histograms\n    showing SCS concentration.'\n  - 'Precision-at-k curve: fraction of top-k SCS pairs that are in top-k empirical\n    confusion pairs, for k=5,10,20,50.'\n  analysis: SCS 是 reasonable proxy（ρ=0.35, 显著）但远非 perfect predictor（ρ<0.5）。 这解释了 SDGD-zero\n    与 SDGD-cal 的 performance gap，并为\"何时用哪种 SDGD 变体\" 提供了 decision criterion：embedding\n    SCS 适合 quick-and-dirty decomposition， empirical calibration 适合 high-stakes applications。\n    论文中作为 2×3 ablation 的 quantitative backing。\n","numLines":768,"startLine":1,"totalLines":768}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HbKGenqy8hfPuzHWxUS11F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the paper and the review context carefully before dispatching reviewers.\n\nThe paper is about \"Pairwise Type Confusability Independently Predicts Extraction Degradation in Training-Free LLM Information Extraction.\" \n\nKey claims:\n1. Pairwise confusability (SCS) independently predicts extraction degradation across NER/RE/ED tasks and two models\n2. Multi-channel degradation model: count → omission, confusability → substitution, approximately additive\n3. Centrality confound in per-type aggregation on homogeneous schemas\n4. SDGD framework reduces type confusion errors by 24-35% but F1 gains not significant\n\n\n5. Now I'm cross-referencing the planned experiments against what's actually presented in the paper—most of the core confusability studies and multi-model validation are covered, though I need to check which experiments were completed versus planned. Now I'm setting up the review process by assigning two reviewers in parallel—one to evaluate the methods and experiments, the other to assess novelty and related work—before running through the full roundtable discussion.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39372,"cache_read_input_tokens":22933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39372},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08912b4a-ab76-4663-b333-b897e4b7593f","uuid":"cd956cc4-0e85-4331-87b9-af5138124246"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HbKGenqy8hfPuzHWxUS11F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've read the paper (10 pages) and the review context (12 planned experiments). The paper covers all 12 planned experiments. Now dispatching two parallel reviewers."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39372,"cache_read_input_tokens":22933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39372},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08912b4a-ab76-4663-b333-b897e4b7593f","uuid":"4b206301-0e6b-43f0-ade3-1f609a0c772d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HbKGenqy8hfPuzHWxUS11F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F4mKoAGQenSYMfBcSrr8sy","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus is **methods and experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\"Pairwise Type Confusability Independently Predicts Extraction Degradation in Training-Free LLM Information Extraction\"\n\nThe paper studies why training-free LLM IE degrades on complex schemas. It isolates \"type confusability\" (embedding cosine similarity between type pairs) from \"type count\" as independent degradation channels. Three contributions: (1) pairwise confusability predicts extraction degradation across NER/RE/ED (r=0.08–0.16); (2) multi-channel degradation model (count→omission, confusability→substitution, additive); (3) centrality confound in per-type aggregation + embedding ablation guidance. SDGD framework reduces type confusion errors 24–35% but F1 gains not statistically significant.\n\n## Key Experimental Results\n\n### Pairwise confusability (§5.2)\n- Few-NERD (66 NER types, Qwen3): pairwise r=0.156 (p=4.6e-12), per-type ρ=−0.293 (p=0.020)\n- MAVEN (168 ED types): MiniLM pairwise r=0.115 (p=2e-34), Qwen3 pairwise r=−0.007 (n.s.)\n- MAVEN per-type: both Qwen3 ρ=+0.189 and MiniLM ρ=+0.208 are POSITIVE (centrality confound)\n- DocRED (96 RE types): Qwen3 r=0.082 (p=0.008), MiniLM r=0.095 (p=0.001) — attenuated\n- Within-count BCS on MAVEN not significant (r=0.12, p=0.18 at count 6)\n\n### 2×2 Factorial (§5.3)\n- Count main effect: ΔF1=−6.3pp, F=8.2, p=0.007\n- Confusability main effect: ΔF1=−5.8pp, F=6.5, p=0.015\n- Interaction: F=1.4, p=0.24, η²=0.03\n- Additive R²=0.38 vs multiplicative R²=0.39\n\n### Error Taxonomy (§5.4)\n- High BCS: 62% substitution, 18% omission\n- Low BCS: 28% substitution, 42% omission\n- Substitution rate increases with count (0.035→0.055)\n\n### Cross-model (§5.5)\n- LLaMA-3.3-70B: pairwise r=0.098 (p=3.2e-5), per-type ρ=−0.215 (p=0.089, not significant)\n- Confusion ratios 6.8–12.5× (vs Qwen3's 9.9–27.5×)\n\n### SDGD (§5.7)\n- SDGD-zero on Few-NERD: F1=0.425 vs single-pass 0.414, ΔF1=+1.1pp, p=0.18 (NOT significant), CI [−1.5, +3.7]\n- SDGD-cal on Few-NERD: F1=0.440, ΔF1=+2.6pp, p=0.09 (NOT significant), CI [−0.8, +6.0]\n- Type confusion reduction: 24% (zero), 35% (cal)\n- Omission increase: 12% for SDGD-zero\n- Per-type splitting (k=66): F1=0.395, BELOW single-pass\n- MAVEN SDGD-zero: relaxed F1=0.240 vs single-pass 0.245 (slightly worse); SDGD-cal: 0.258 (+1.3pp, not significant)\n- Random batching (k=8): F1=0.418, SDGD-zero only +0.7pp over random\n\n### SCS vs Empirical Confusion (§5.8)\n- Qwen3 SCS vs empirical: ρ=0.35, top-10 overlap 50%\n- MiniLM: ρ=0.22, top-10 overlap 30%\n\n### 2×3 Embedding Ablation (§5.8, Table 12)\n- No single embedding dominates across datasets\n- Qwen3 per-type works for cross-domain (Few-NERD), fails same-domain (MAVEN pairwise)\n- MiniLM pairwise works for same-domain (MAVEN), fails cross-domain per-type\n\n## Experiment Coverage Reference\nThe planned experiments from the design document include 12 experiments (exp-004 through exp-015). The paper covers all of them:\n- MAVEN full study, DocRED scaling, Count×Confusability interaction, Error taxonomy, LLaMA validation, SDGD-zero on Few-NERD and MAVEN, SDGD-cal on Few-NERD and MAVEN, Random batching ablation, Per-type splitting ablation, SCS vs empirical confusion validation.\n\nFewRel is mentioned in the abstract/intro as one of four datasets but results are sparse in the paper (only Table 12 mentions FewRel with \"Δ=21–50pp\" for MiniLM per-type). Full FewRel results seem absent.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nProvide a structured review covering:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (bullet points, focus on methods/experiments)\n3. **Weaknesses** (bullet points, focus on methods/experiments)\n4. **Questions to Authors** (specific, numbered)\n5. **Minor Issues**\n6. **Preliminary Score** (1-6) with justification\n7. **Confidence** (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous. Pay attention to:\n- Statistical rigor (effect sizes, p-values, confidence intervals, multiple comparisons)\n- Experimental design (controls, confounds, sample sizes)\n- Whether the claimed contributions are actually supported by the data\n- Reproducibility concerns\n- Missing experiments or analyses\n- Whether SDGD results are honestly framed given they're not statistically significant\n- The gap between \"type confusion error reduction\" and actual F1 improvement\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39372,"cache_read_input_tokens":22933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39372},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08912b4a-ab76-4663-b333-b897e4b7593f","uuid":"30a8bd5b-2d07-49c1-b624-fec9de16d9a4"}
